# Trivy ignore file — rhel-9 base-image tuples ONLY
#
# Applied by .github/workflows/build-base-images.yml (step "Compute Trivy
# ignore files") on top of the root .trivyignore, and only for
# distro=rhel distro_version=9. It never masks these CVE IDs on another distro.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# krb5-libs 1.21.1-10.el9_8.1 — 14 HIGH CVEs, fix not yet in the UBI repos
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# EXPIRES: 2026-12-15 (each line's exp: makes Trivy re-flag it automatically)
#
# Why suppress a CVE Trivy marks `fixed`: the fix (1.21.1-10.el9_9.2) is not
# reachable from a UBI build. As of 2026-11-15 the public UBI9 BaseOS repo
# (cdn-ubi.redhat.com/content/public/ubi/dist/ubi9/9/x86_64/baseos/os) carries
# only krb5-libs-1.21.1-10.el9_8.1, so `microdnf upgrade -y` on
# ubi-minimal:9.9 reports "Nothing to do" (PR #1671 CI). `ignore-unfixed`
# cannot help because Trivy reads the RHEL advisory, which does list a fix.
#
# Exposure: these are KDC (krb5kdc) and kadmind *server* flaws: DoS, memory
# leaks, request alteration, CAMMAC auth-indicator alteration. The image ships
# only the client library krb5-libs, which comes preinstalled in ubi-minimal
# (the Dockerfile adds just ca-certificates, shadow-utils, and sudo). It
# installs neither krb5-server nor krb5-workstation, and it runs no KDC or
# kadmind.
#
# Remove when: the UBI9 BaseOS repo publishes krb5-libs >= 1.21.1-10.el9_9.2.
# Verify with:
#   curl -s <repo>/repodata/repomd.xml -> primary.xml.gz | grep krb5-libs-
# then delete this block and confirm the rhel-9 Trivy gate is green without it.
# Tracking: #1669.
CVE-2026-107364 exp:2026-12-15
